From 063f71b8c277dd613b36dd577fe955806a3bbf6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:32:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix: Group-safe partial merge + solo-group auto-greed
 (I-137)

- Merge only plain items (not FFA/conditional/quest-flagged) - merged
  copies of per-player-list items were invisible and unlootable in the
  merged window, leaving unlootedCount stuck above zero so the main
  corpse never became skinnable (I-137 recurrence)
- Mark merged items looted on the source corpse instead of clear(), so
  leftover FFA/conditional/quest items stay individually lootable
- Never touch corpses that were already opened (loot windows / rolls
  reference their slots) or that are round-robin assigned to another
  group member
- In roll-based loot methods, leave over-threshold items for the group
  roll; exception: sole-member groups with AOELoot.AutoGreedSolo, where
  merged items enter the merged window's roll and resolve instantly
- Auto-greed loot rolls when the player is the only group member
  (AOELoot.AutoGreedSolo, default on)
- Quest items go to bags with stock StoreLootItem bookkeeping instead
  of being destroyed with the source loot

